610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,17,18,1251,9417,264,4614,13,8886,1697,62030,6078,448,518,3245,825,1008,1697,13,3555,374,279,8028,3204,1372,315,1424,927,2050,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\n23 people attend a party. Each person shakes hands with at least one other person. What is the minimum possible number of handshakes?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9338d52fc261109439117fccf398554aa3f462a3ddafc2a70382a8c500923730"},"seconds":19.10633420944214,"seed":1129068096525066857,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the minimum possible number of handshakes in a scenario where 23 people each shake hands with at least one other person, we can use the concept of a graph where each person is a vertex and each handshake is an edge.\n\n1. **Understanding the Graph Representation:**\n   - Each person is represented as a vertex.\n   - A handshake between two people is represented as an edge connecting two vertices.\n\n2. **Minimum Handshakes Condition:**\n   - Each person must shake hands with at least one other person, which means each vertex must have a degree of at least 1.\n\n3. **Constructing the Graph:**\n   - To have the minimum number of handshakes, we need to construct a graph where every vertex has exactly one edge.\n   - This is achieved by creating a graph where each vertex is connected to exactly one other vertex, forming a set of disjoint edges.\n\n4. **Number of Edges:**\n   - Since each person shakes hands with exactly one other person, the graph will consist of disjoint edges.\n   - For 23 people, we can form 11 pairs and have one person left out (since 23 is odd, one person will not have a pair).\n\n5. **Calculating the Minimum Number of Handshakes:**\n   - Each pair contributes 1 handshake.\n   - With 11 pairs, the number of handshakes is 11.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible number of handshakes is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{11}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{11}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
